PianoDpu is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). Level 1 only: a read-only survey. What it takes from other
work, and from where:

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoAudio/PianoAudio.cpp (sha256 cb0499f7fa02dec2919101843c70a1d3d7b9eed389c77625ac032782321f6a8a): the kext's shape
    (probe gate on the boot argument, a survey thread, the post-mortem stage word, MMIO pages mapped on demand and loaded with an
    explicit ldr, one summary property, repeated samples), re-written for this driver.
  package/PianoAudio/AudioSurvey.h (sha256 a1c982501ad281c1a59b10de809cf50177d9c91b455d4bab8528fbfa256dea0e) and
  package/PianoWifi/WifiSurvey.h (sha256 41a9703bf079dfd4f86fe5073399c788725d43e7dc0ad4306b36ffd16c9aa219): surveySmmu / s2crType
    re-expressed for the DPU's four streams, with the bank's CBAR/CBA2R/SCTLR/TCR/TCR2/TTBR0/MAIR0/FSR (PianoWifi read a matching
    bank's SCTLR on this SMMU) and a route verdict.
  package/PianoAudio/tests/audio_host.cpp (sha256 dfe2b7d81ac2cbe4a0633bf4441107c192a352cb448e0df663a74e0709298833): the
    register-model harness (Soc, CHECK), re-used in tests/dpu_host.cpp.

UniXNU community code (facts only, no code copied; read for what other SM8x50 ports read and what they measured):
  GopFramebuffer (unixnu-research/GopFramebuffer, BSD-2-Clause-Patent) NativeLegacyDisplay.cpp (sha256
    e30354b7255fda259a25f3f7f22ecaff8c1c584196f8e54e6c402c03022d5770): the address-only flip (SRC0_ADDR + YSTRIDE0 of the scanning
    pipes, CTL FLUSH, no START in video mode), its fence rule and IOSurface windows. The donor of B1b (docs/drivers/dpu.md section 4).
  ShengUfs (unixnu-research/ShengUfs, BSD-2-Clause-Patent sources) NativeUfs.cpp (sha256
    257fe82d29e80708f7eff65842d3382f3cff6d81416686452bceb776a3813132): the display stream's SMMU readout and its in-place translation
    window (dpuEnable, native_ufs_dpu_map), measured on SM8550 under the same hypervisor family. The donor of B1b's SMMU step.
  UniXNU-sheng (BSD-2-Clause-Patent) package/DisplayTimingProbe.cpp (sha256
    2f65657b55a766ec18de8d1cb059ffdde7f59daefae6b6849fa0bcd93b31324f): the frame counter read twice for the refresh (its INTF engine
    word at +0x6c is not the timing engine enable; this survey reads +0x0).
  hackios-xnu-kernel-k90 (APSL 2.0, an SM8750 phone): facts only (the display clocks must be checked before an MDSS load; the
    branch list), no code read into this package.

Specifications only (no code, comment or table copied; GPL-2.0): the Ubuntu piano kernel (unixnu-research/ubuntu-ref/kernel, branch
piano/dev, 7f8d6bedde479a01f4a05d6d0581b43c7fd20a01): drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_12_0_sm8750.h (sha256
114e33e2b01d55edeaf7940c16742327babb3bf9780e910596f61944fb999e82; block bases, interrupt bits), dpu_hw_sspp.c, dpu_hw_ctl.c,
dpu_hw_lm.c, dpu_hw_dspp.c, dpu_hw_intf.c, dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c, dpu_hw_merge3d.c, dpu_hw_interrupts.c, dpu_hwio.h, dpu_hw_catalog.c
